# Damage numbers only in the playground (#321, sub-task 321.4): in an original level a hit that damages an NPC shows
# no number - no `damage.number` event and damageNumbers.visible 0. Companion of damage-numbers.xrs (the playground case).
#
# Runs on the test save mvp-goblin-fight (#70: a goblin ahead in a corridor):
#   .\scripts\dev\xrs-run.ps1 damage-numbers-off
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -VrSim idle -Sequence damage-numbers-off -Save mvp-goblin-fight
# The hit is `player.dodamage goblin_base_0036 5` (damageCharacter(), the path every damage source ends in). The eye
# images are not compared: the goblin's hurt animation alone changes the largest channel by ~236 (a first run), so a
# picture cannot tell a number from the animation - the event and the status value do.
@sim idle
@save mvp-goblin-fight
@args --loadslot 0

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false

goblin_base_0036.setspeed 0
place goblin_base_0036 80
lookat goblin_base_0036
@frames 60

@mark
player.dodamage goblin_base_0036 5
@assert damageNumbers.visible eq 0
@shot during-hit       # for the reviewer's eye: no number over the goblin
@frames 60
@assert damageNumbers.visible eq 0
@nolog damage\.number
@assert errors eq 0
